		<ParagraphStyleRange AppliedParagraphStyle="ParagraphStyle/A4 V%3aSubhead Large">
			<CharacterStyleRange AppliedCharacterStyle="CharacterStyle/$ID/[No character style]">
				<Content>Victorian Owners Gold Card (VOGC)</Content>
				<Br />
			</CharacterStyleRange>
		</ParagraphStyleRange>
		<ParagraphStyleRange AppliedParagraphStyle="ParagraphStyle/A4 V%3aBody">
			<CharacterStyleRange AppliedCharacterStyle="CharacterStyle/$ID/[No character style]">
				<Content>The VOGC program continues to reward owners 
who support the state’s racing industry by granting them a range of benefits and privileges at all Victorian race clubs. </Content>
				<Br />
				<Content>Work continued throughout FY25 on the development of a digital ticketing platform designed to centralise raceday ticketing and enhance the raceday experience for owners. Subsequently launched in September 2025, the project is being delivered in partnership with the Thoroughbred Racehorse Owners Association (TROA) and with the support of the Victoria Racing Club (VRC), Melbourne Racing Club (MRC), Moonee Valley Racing Club (MVRC), Country Racing Victoria (CRV) and Southside Racing. The initiative is made possible thanks to a significant investment from the State Government’s Victorian Racing Industry Fund (VRIF). </Content>
				<Br />
			</CharacterStyleRange>
		</ParagraphStyleRange>
		<ParagraphStyleRange AppliedParagraphStyle="ParagraphStyle/A4 V%3aSubhead Large" SpaceBefore="11.338582677165356" SpaceAfter="1.4173228346456694">
			<CharacterStyleRange AppliedCharacterStyle="CharacterStyle/$ID/[No character style]">
				<Content>Victorian Owners and Breeders Incentive Scheme (VOBIS)</Content>
				<Br />
			</CharacterStyleRange>
		</ParagraphStyleRange>
		<ParagraphStyleRange AppliedParagraphStyle="ParagraphStyle/A4 V%3aBody">
			<CharacterStyleRange AppliedCharacterStyle="CharacterStyle/$ID/[No character style]">
				<Content>The VOBIS program remains an integral component of Victoria’s vibrant racing and breeding industries, rewarding those who breed, buy, own and race thoroughbreds in the state.  </Content>
				<Br />
				<Content>In FY25, more than $14.07 million in VOBIS prizemoney, bonuses and vouchers was distributed to participants, making VOBIS the richest incentive program in Australian racing.</Content>
				<Br />
				<Content>Open exclusively to VOBIS Gold and VOBIS Platinum horses, the Premier Race Series offered $5.5 million in prizemoney, bonuses and vouchers across 19 premium races.</Content>
				<Br />
				<Content>Offering in excess of $7.5 million in vouchers each season, the VOBIS Platinum program continues to support owners, breeders, trainers and syndicators by incentivising reinvestment in the Victorian industry. Since its inception, more than $6 million in VOBIS Platinum vouchers has been won, with $3.5 million redeemed at the conclusion of FY25. Of that figure, $2.11 million was redeemed on Victorian-bred horses at the yearling sales, $1.2 million was used to offset the cost of a VOBIS Sires service fee and more than $200,000 was reinvested with a syndication company.</Content>
				<Br />
				<Content>In FY25, 71 stallions were nominated to the VOBIS Sires program, ensuring their progeny are eligible for the lucrative VOBIS Platinum bonuses and vouchers. Another key takeout from FY25 is that upgrades for 2022-born foals to the VOBIS Gold and VOBIS Platinum programs increased by 5%, reversing a 
three-year decline.</Content>
				<Br />
				<Content>A comprehensive review of the VOBIS program was undertaken in FY25, comprising customer research, stakeholder submissions and analysis of racing and VOBIS data. The results of the review are being analysed with a view to implementing changes 
at the start of the 2026-27 racing season.</Content>
				<Br />
			</CharacterStyleRange>
		</ParagraphStyleRange>
